    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0682" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1229/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Higgins</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">for the
                        British Ambassador</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lenox,
                            Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-10-10"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">October 10, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 195.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had the honor to communicate to His
                    Majesty’s secretary of state for foreign affairs the fact that the United States
                    Government were willing to forego provisionally their extraterritorial rights in
                    Zanzibar, which you notified to me in your note No. 489 of July 27.</p>
                <p>I am now instructed by Sir Edward Grey to express to you the thanks of His
                    Majesty’s Government for the courteous manner in which their desires on the
                    subject have been met.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Higgins</hi>,</signed><lb/>(For
                    the Ambassador.)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
